Z||000032||falconhulk||12-06-2001||08:17 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>In Jersey we have Tastykakes, Scrapple (don't ask), Pork roll and Strohmen bread and of course an original Philly Cheesesteak.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Huh?  I live in WV and have lived in MD most of my life.  I work in VA.  In all those states you can get tastykakes, Scrapple, and <BR>Strohmen bread.  Original Philly Cheesesteak<BR>can be had proabably anywhere on the east coast but with varying quality.  Pork roll I am not sure what you are talking about but if its a roll thats about 4 to 5 inches in diameter and around a foot long they are very common in the stores all over as well.  Not trying to prove ya wrong but its nice to know that things are available elsewhere.  The mid atlantic area does have UTZ chips that are not available in most states.<BR>||||reg||1
