Z||000035||Raydar||12-06-2001||12:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by annieL:<BR><B>I was wondering what can you get in your state/town that no one else can get?<P>In Jersey we have Tastykakes, Scrapple (don't ask), Pork roll and Strohmen bread and of course an original Philly Cheesesteak.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>And you can also get veal loaf. (For the uninitiated, it's deli sandwich meat.)<P>We can't. <BR>Asking for veal loaf in Atlanta gets you a puzzled look and, "Whut is veeeeeal loaf?"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>We've got grits in the South, but you can <I>have</I> them.<BR>Grits just suck. MHO, of course.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
